{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED on exact head d52dfbfa4b33321534ba2879ea3f170b971dc45b / primary artifact f4641960.\n\nArchitecture: this head affects layer 6, Projections and queries (internal/statusview), and layer 7, CLI/MCP surfaces and their references. It changes a projection contract: an omitted WorkQuery.stale no longer means include, terminal stale rows are omitted by default, the MCP stale enum gains summary, and the public JSON shapes gain closed_stale_omitted, retired_artifacts, and world_stale_artifacts. docs/reference/architecture.md explicitly defines projection contracts to include names, types, limits, cursor behavior, and omission rules, and AGENTS.md requires any contract-changing head to update that page and publish its candidate artifact at the same head. This head does neither. Add the precise additive fields and changed default/omission rule to docs/reference/architecture.md and publish its exact-head artifact, then request fresh review. No kernel, storage, host-binding, fold, or authority semantics changed.\n\nSecurity: no security defect found. The read path still validates the actor before filtering; StaleSummary changes selection only and cannot widen actor scope or write authority. Explicit stale=include/only/exclude and named statuses recover the detailed rows; listed rows retain their stale field. Retired and superseded-world artifacts remain separately counted and individually rendered on the gs status artifact rows. No secrets, signatures, custody, or untrusted payload parsing moved.\n\nSimplification: the localized selection changes and explicit summary policy are a reasonable minimum for the requested presentation while preserving old explicit modes. Keeping summary as a named typed value makes cursor/filter behavior and documentation clearer than a hidden empty-value special case. No removable implementation fluff found.\n\nConditions and regression evidence: default status/status-wait/work summarization, explicit-detail